id: pm-zzylb9
title: "Outcome milestone: measured self-improvement — every shipped improvement closes an evidence-selected, gated, re-measured cycle"
description: Graduate pm from a project that measures quality to a project whose own immutable evidence selects the next improvement and proves the resulting change moved a declared outcome metric. This milestone is an outcome gate over the existing recursive self-improvement programme rather than a new implementation programme.
type: Milestone
status: open
priority: 2
tags[7]: "area:self-improvement",context-management,"horizon:far",milestone,outcome,recursive-improvement,roadmap
created_at: "2026-08-14T14:34:47.581Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-14T14:34:47.581Z"
deadline: "2029-12-31T00:00:00.000Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 43200
acceptance_criteria: Every shipped improvement cycle begins from a versioned evidence-ranked candidate rather than filing recency; Every cycle records baseline target gate decision landed change and post-change measurement as reconstructable immutable evidence; At least three consecutive production cycles improve their declared metric without weakening another blocking invariant; Candidate selection false-positive rate cycle lead time escaped-defect rate and tokens per completed cycle have published baselines and ratchets; A third party can replay any completed cycle through the public SDK and independently reproduce its verdict
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make recursive self-improvement a measured outcome rather than a narrated aspiration
value: The project continuously improves from its own evidence while preserving human review and immutable accountability
impact: Turns history recurrence context economics and assurance into one closed improvement loop
outcome: A repeatable auditable self-improvement capability that demonstrates sustained measured gains
why_now: The recursive self-improvement epic and its delivery slices now exist but the portfolio has no outcome gate beyond universal-domain capability
parent: pm-doxj
risk: high
confidence: low
